  "id": "congruity-theory",
  "term": "congruity theory",
  "definition": "Congruity theory, as described here in the context of role congruity, is the idea that people can be judged negatively when their behavior does not fit stereotyped social roles. In this gender context, women pursuing career success or men taking on more domestic labor may face backlash or economic penalties because they are seen as crossing expected spheres.",
